===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*bʰel-|id=blow}}
From {{inh|en|enm|bole}}, {{m|enm|bul}}, {{m|enm|bule}}, from a conflation of {{der|en|ang|bula||bull, steer}} and {{der|en|non|boli}}, both from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*bulô||bull}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*bʰl̥no-}}, from {{m|ine-pro|*bʰel-||to blow, swell up}}. Cognate with {{cog|fy|bolle}}, {{cog|nl|bul}}, {{cog|nds-de|Bull}}, {{cog|de|Bulle}}, {{cog|sv|bulla}}; also {{cog|sga|ball||limb}}, {{cog|la|follis||bellows, leather bag}}, {{cog|txh|βόλινθος||wild bull|sc=Grek}}, [[Macedonian]] ''[[вол]]'' (vol, "ox"), [[Slovene]] ''[[vol]]'' ("ox"), {{cog|sq|buall|t=buffalo}} or related {{m|sq|bolle||testicles}}, {{cog|grc|φαλλός||penis}}.

